<%# THE PANE ALONE: ModelsController#show's answer when Turbo asks for the `model_stage` frame. It
    renders in layouts/turbo_rails/frame (this app's copy, which carries the page's real <head>), and
    it sets the page's own title because Turbo copies the response's <title> into the page when it
    records the promoted visit. %>
<% content_for :title, "#{@model.title} — Tinkerex" %>
<%= render "models/stage", model: @model, stage: @stage, viewer: @viewer %>
